# useMoveImageOptions

Turns the `moveImage` option of a background wrapper (`true`, `false` or a partial object) into explicit flags for each input: dragging with the mouse and dragging with one finger. `CropperBackgroundWrapper` uses it to configure `TransformableImage`.

## Signature

```ts
function useMoveImageOptions(moveImage: MoveImageOptions | boolean): DefinedMoveImageOptions;

interface MoveImageOptions {
	touch?: boolean;
	mouse?: boolean;
}

interface DefinedMoveImageOptions {
	touch: boolean;
	mouse: boolean;
}
```

## Parameters

| Input                | Result                           |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `true`               | `{ touch: true, mouse: true }`   |
| `false` or undefined | `{ touch: false, mouse: false }` |
| `{ mouse: false }`   | `{ touch: true, mouse: false }`  |
| `{}`                 | `{ touch: true, mouse: true }`   |

In an object, a missing key is enabled.

## Return value

A new `DefinedMoveImageOptions` object with both flags set.

## When to call it

Anywhere. It is a pure function with no effects. When its input is a prop, wrap the call in `$derived` so the result follows the prop.

## Example

A custom background wrapper that maps the options onto `TransformableImage`, as `CropperBackgroundWrapper` does:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import {
		TransformableImage,
		useMoveImageOptions,
		useRotateImageOptions,
		useScaleImageOptions,
		type CropperBackgroundWrapperProps
	} from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	let {
		cropper,
		moveImage = true,
		scaleImage = true,
		rotateImage = false,
		children,
		class: className,
		style,
		timeout,
		disabled
	}: CropperBackgroundWrapperProps = $props();

	const moveOptions = $derived(useMoveImageOptions(moveImage));
	const scaleOptions = $derived(useScaleImageOptions(scaleImage));
	const rotateOptions = $derived(useRotateImageOptions(rotateImage));
</script>

<TransformableImage
	class={className}
	{style}
	onTransform={cropper.transformImage}
	onTransformEnd={cropper.transformImageEnd}
	touchMove={moveOptions.touch}
	mouseMove={moveOptions.mouse}
	touchScale={scaleOptions.touch}
	wheelScale={scaleOptions.wheel}
	touchRotate={rotateOptions.touch}
	disabled={cropper.getTransitions().active || disabled}
	preventDefault={!disabled}
	{timeout}
>
	{@render children?.()}
</TransformableImage>
```

Pass it to a cropper with `backgroundWrapperComponent={MyBackgroundWrapper}`.

## Differences from React

React memoizes the result with `useMemo`, which makes it a hook. Here it is a plain function, and `$derived` provides the memoization when you need it. The name is kept for parity with react-advanced-cropper.
